LevlPrep — licensing
====================

This repository contains two different kinds of work, under two different
licences. Which one applies depends on what you are copying.


1. CONTENT — Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Applies to the study material: the question banks and their explanations, the
study notes, the Organic Chemistry lessons, notes and mechanism walkthroughs,
the branching scenarios, the glossary, mnemonics, skill sheets, flow diagrams
and body-map descriptions. In file terms, everything under:

    nremt/assets/*.json
    nremt/study-notes.html, glossary.html, mnemonics.html, skillsheets.html,
      flowcharts.html, scenario-sim.html, body-map.html   (their text content)
    ochem/notes/, ochem/lessons/, ochem/mechanisms/        (their text content)
    ochem/assets/practice-bank.json

You are free to share and adapt this material for non-commercial purposes,
with attribution to LevlPrep (https://levlprep.com) and an indication of any
changes made. You may not use it for commercial purposes.

Full text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/legalcode
Summary:   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/

The non-commercial term is the point of it. The core question bank and course
material on this site are free, permanently, with no ads, and the licence
exists so that the material
cannot be repackaged and sold back to students. Using it to teach — in a
classroom, a study group, or a course you do not charge for — is exactly what
it is for, and needs no permission beyond the attribution.


